	"title"		"SpireTalk: Living Ancients"
	"description"		"[b]The Ancients talk back.[/b] Every Ancient and the Merchant answers you in their own voice, remembers what you said last run, asks things of you, and hands you a relic that grows with the friendship. Runs on your own API key, inside the game. No account, no server, nothing to sign up for.

[b]Both art styles supported:[/b] vanilla out of the box; with [b]AncientWaifus[/b] + [b]Merchant2CuteII[/b] installed, the mod's own paintings switch to the waifu look automatically.

[h1]What you get[/h1]

[h3]Talk[/h3]
A [b]Talk[/b] option on every Ancient's page and a [b]Talk[/b] button in the shop. Three lines per visit: pick a suggested reply or type your own. Neow, Orobas, Nonupeipe, Pael, Darv, Tanx, Tezcatara, Vakuu and the Merchant each have their own persona, their own values, and their own memory.

[h3]They remember[/h3]
What you told Neow stays with Neow, run after run (per save profile; can be switched off). Earlier visits are kept as short notes, and a Memories page in the settings lets you read, edit, add or delete what each of them remembers. Affection moves with every line you say, judged by that NPC's own values: hostile / stranger / friendly / close / devoted.

[h3]Deals[/h3]
An NPC may ask something of you when you arrive: [i]reach the next act alive[/i], [i]no potions until then[/i], [i]spend 150 gold at my shop[/i]... Answer with a button. The terms come from the mod, so the game can always check them. Kept: affection and gold. Broken: a disappointed line, nothing more. Open deals sit under your relics.

[h3]Keepsakes[/h3]
Once an NPC likes you they press their keepsake into your hands: a relic with levels I / II / III that follow the relationship and rise mid-run the moment the number crosses. Every deal you keep engraves it. Nine of them, one per NPC, each in that NPC's manner: Neow heals you after fights and catches you at 1 HP once per run; Tanx sharpens your first attack; Vakuu lends Strength for blood; the Merchant keeps a ledger of discounts.

[h3]Ancient relics on the shelf[/h3]
An Ancient who likes you may leave one of [i]their own[/i] relics with the Merchant for you, relics otherwise found only in their halls, priced like a rare.

[h3]Epilogue[/h3]
When a run ends, the NPC who knew you best says a few words about it on the game-over screen: the deals, where you fell, how you won.

[h3]On the road[/h3]
Up to two new events per run, each with its own painting. [b]The Overturned Cart[/b]: the Merchant's cart has tipped over; help (and get a potion and a discount), pocket a relic (and pay for it at every shop this run), or walk on. [b]An Ancient by the Road[/b]: an Ancient you have talked to sits by the path, weary; give what they ask or sit with them, and a card gets upgraded. They speak in their own voice, and remember it next time.

[h3]Real rewards, honest rules[/h3]
Relic reroll, gold, healing, a potion, a shop discount. The mod validates every reward against fixed rules and applies it through the game's own commands. The AI only ever narrates; it never touches your run directly.

[h1]Setup in one minute[/h1]
[olist]
[*] Click the mushie in the top-right corner of the main menu.
[*] Pick a source: OpenRouter, a local Ollama, or anything that speaks the OpenAI API.
[*] Paste your key (Ollama needs none), pick a model from the list, press [b]Test[/b]. Start a run. Talk.
[/olist]
The NPCs run on the [url=https://github.com/lovetimo0421/yumina-oss]Yumina engine[/url] inside the game, and the mod connects to nothing but the endpoint you configure. Each NPC is a Yumina card (a JSON file); drop your own into [i]%APPDATA%\SlayTheSpire2\spiretalk\cards\[/i] to replace a persona.

[h1]Good to know[/h1]
[list]
[*] Languages: English and Simplified Chinese. The NPCs answer in Chinese when the game runs in Simplified Chinese, in English otherwise.
[*] Requires [b]BaseLib[/b]. Works with [b]Ancient Affection[/b] (shares its affection number) and with character skin mods.
[*] Temperament setting: lenient / normal / strict.
[*] Single player only.
[*] The cover and the road-encounter paintings are generated art, redrawn from the game's own characters.
[/list]"
	"changenote"		"0.4.2 - NPCs no longer repeat themselves: earlier visits are remembered as short notes instead of their old lines, and phrases already said are cut; new Memories page in settings to read, edit, add or delete what each NPC remembers; rewards now arrive after the NPC finishes speaking; the Merchant in the overturned-cart art now wears his mask; the deals bar sits below your relics instead of over them"
